          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Misconceptions and Legacy</strong><br>\nOver the centuries, Sappho's life and sexuality have been the subject of much debate and many misconceptions. The term \"lesbian\" originates from the island of Lesbos and is associated with Sappho due to the themes of female affection in her poetry. However, translating these relationships into modern terms of sexuality is controversial among scholars.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Preservation of Sappho's Work</strong><br>\nThe preservation of Sappho's work has been a patchwork process, with pieces appearing in unexpected places. Some were found in Egyptian garbage heaps, preserved on scraps of papyrus, while others survived through quotations in the works of later writers and scholars, intrigued by her reputation and the beauty of her compositions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Sappho's Enduring Mystery</strong><br>\nDespite the loss of most of her lyrical oeuvre, Sappho remains an enigmatic figure in literary history. Her work still resonates due to its emotional authenticity and its evocative exploration of human relationships. The fragments that survive hint at the vast talent of a poet who was once able to capture the complexities of human emotion in just a few, perfectly chosen words.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
